WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.690
- This is a Ford Model T from 1911

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:05.460
and under the hood, it's hiding a secret.

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:07.950
See, this car is actually
an electric vehicle.

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:10.860
It was recently converted from
gas to electric by this man,

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:13.530
80 year old former electic
model engineer, Robert Knight.

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:16.200
And it's not just Robert or antique Fords.

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.540
As EV adoption increases around the globe,

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:20.760
a string of startups
have emerged with the aim

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:24.780
of retrofitting and upcycling
gas cars into electric ones.

00:00:26.271 --> 00:00:28.854
(gentle music)

00:00:40.630 --> 00:00:43.530
Okay, so firstly, what's
it take to convert a car?

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:46.650
Well, as Robert found out, it's
both simple and really hard.

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:48.660
- So the initial conversion was a year,

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:51.810
but since then I've been
modifying it and modifying it,

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:53.519
and I've had mistake after mistake.

00:00:53.519 --> 00:00:56.070
- [George Downs] Step one
is to drain the fuel tank

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:57.960
and completely remove the engine block.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:00:59.880
That can create a space where batteries

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:01.860
and an electric motor can be installed.

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:04.560
Next is the task of hooking
that motor up to the drivetrain

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:06.750
and wiring in a battery management system.

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:08.460
After that, it's just a case of hooking

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:11.940
up the new drivetrain to the
controls, or in Robert's case,

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:14.130
installing these various switches.

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:16.590
Ford purists, look away now.

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:18.540
- I've had one or two adverse comments

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:23.003
about wrecking a 1911 Ford Model T.

00:01:23.003 --> 00:01:24.720
- [George Downs] Robert
tells me he's managed

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:27.570
to get around 25 miles of
range out of his conversion,

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:30.780
which is just enough to get him
to the local shops and back.

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:33.900
And the conversion cost, under $2,000,

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:36.510
most of which came from
the sale of the engine.

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:38.236
- So it's trivial, absolutely trivial.

00:01:38.236 --> 00:01:39.960
- [George Downs] So if it's possible

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:42.390
to do a relatively cheap
conversion yourself,

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:44.190
is it possible to make
money from doing it?

00:01:44.190 --> 00:01:46.050
To find out, I've come to UK based

00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:48.630
EV upcycling startup, Lunaz.

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:51.660
Each of these cars may look
like an original classic car

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:53.550
but they've actually all
been completely stripped

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:55.350
and rebuilt from the ground up

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:57.813
with a brand new electric powertrain.

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:01.729
That's the only bit of that
car I can afford to touch.

00:02:01.729 --> 00:02:04.410
That's because the starting
price for the conversion

00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:08.610
of these classics is
around $370,000 and up,

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:09.990
which is around the same price

00:02:09.990 --> 00:02:12.390
as buying a competition condition classic.

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:15.120
But it's not just classic
cars that Lunaz is upcycling.

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:17.430
They're also taking
commercial fleet vehicles

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:18.720
like these garbage trucks

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:21.360
and running them through a
similar upcycling process.

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:22.920
Here's CEO David Lorenz.

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:24.240
- Some of the trucks behind me today,

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:26.370
these are seven year old vehicles.

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:27.990
They have done a hundred thousand miles

00:02:27.990 --> 00:02:29.100
over their seven year life.

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:32.340
They were tried and tested by
the OEM for a million miles.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:35.460
Fundamentally, it is so
logical to upcycle the vehicle

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:37.380
that already exists to
clean their powertrain.

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:39.030
- David told me that for Lunaz,

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:42.030
upcycling actually presents
a faster route to market

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:44.190
and means that their
trucks can be thousands

00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:46.740
of dollars cheaper than
buying a new EV equivalent.

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:48.690
- We do 80% less work.

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:51.450
All of the bumpers,
windscreen wipers, mechanisms,

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:53.070
we don't have to face these challenges.

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:54.900
These vehicles have
been so well engineered

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:55.733
in the first place.

00:02:55.733 --> 00:02:57.600
- [George Downs] The main
reason David founded Lunaz was

00:02:57.600 --> 00:02:59.400
that he believes by upcycling

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:02.430
you can remove more carbon
dioxide from the loop

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:03.930
than if you buy new EVs.

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:05.940
- If you go and replace 5,000 vehicles

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:07.830
with clean air powertrain vehicles,

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:09.450
that's fantastic in one sense.

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:12.060
But what happens to
your old 5,000 vehicles?

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:13.740
They're gonna end up on cargo ships.

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:15.450
They're gonna end up in
less privileged countries,

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:16.710
and they're gonna sweat longer hours

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:18.060
than you were using them for,

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:19.730
naturally producing more emissions.

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:22.440
- So if retrofitting and
upcycling could potentially

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:25.530
present a faster path towards
hitting climate targets,

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:27.780
and there are businesses out
there making money from it,

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:29.820
why aren't more OEMs doing it?

00:03:29.820 --> 00:03:31.260
Well, companies like Ford and GM

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:33.750
have made some tentative
steps into retrofitting

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:36.450
by offering electric versions
of certain components.

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:38.940
But according to Patrick
Hertzke, automotive analyst

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:42.270
and partner at McKinsey,
automakers have bigger fish to fry.

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:45.060
- They have their hands full scaling up

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:48.450
standard EV production,
getting gigafactory supply

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:51.000
of batteries within their supply chain,

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:52.620
trying to drive costs down.

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:55.200
- Another reason is that
releasing retrofitting options

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:58.140
could potentially sabotage
sales of new cars,

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:01.200
as some customers may choose
to retrofit instead of replace.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:02.880
But possibly the biggest reason is

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:04.950
that it can be very hard to turn a profit

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:07.110
from retrofitting everyday vehicles.

00:04:07.110 --> 00:04:08.550
After all, while these classic cars

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:10.920
and garbage trucks may
look very different,

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:14.010
they're both expensive enough
to make retrofitting worth it.

00:04:14.010 --> 00:04:16.980
The classic cars retain value
and there's economies of scale

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:20.220
in retrofitting a small
fleet of identical vehicles.

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:21.240
Or as David said...

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:24.000
- There is no vehicle
that can't be upcycled

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:25.260
to clean air powertrain.

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:27.720
It's just, is it a cost
effective solution?

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:28.920
What is the cost to this?

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:29.970
- But there may be something

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:31.620
that could help shift the balance

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:34.410
and make retrofitting
more popular; subsidies.

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:36.450
- The extent that these retrofitters

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:39.510
can fully access
additional subsidy schemes

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:43.230
or regulatory encouragement
can certainly have an impact.

00:04:43.230 --> 00:04:44.910
- And if you wanna know
what that might look like,

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:46.770
it's already happening in France.

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:49.290
There, retrofitted electric
vehicles are eligible

00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:52.050
for a few thousand dollars
in government subsidies,

00:04:52.050 --> 00:04:54.090
and you have companies
like Renault teaming up

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:56.490
with retrofitter R-FIT
to offer conversions

00:04:56.490 --> 00:04:58.710
of cheaper classic vehicles and startups

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:01.920
like Transition-One offering
conversions on light city cars.

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:04.080
But here's the thing, even with subsidies

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:06.450
it can be really hard to turn a profit.

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:07.950
While I was reporting this story,

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:10.560
Transition-One stopped
trading as the company said

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:13.200
it no longer had the
financial means to continue.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:15.660
So without significant
government incentives

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:17.550
it's unlikely you'll see OEMs getting

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:20.040
into the retrofitting game anytime soon.

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:22.230
But keep an eye on those
retrofitting startups

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:24.690
'cause they can have a lot
of vehicles to work with.

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:26.970
While EVs may have made up 10%

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:29.760
of all new car sales last
year, they're still a fraction

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:33.832
of the estimated 1.4 billion
vehicles on the planet.

00:05:33.832 --> 00:05:36.415
(gentle music)

